    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i just had to do a rumenotomy on one of my heifers because of a blockage. can u give me a list of what i should be looking for in terms of recovery and signs of infection over the next week? also what should i feed her once she starts acting normal again?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Monitor the heifer continuously for signs of fever, a swollen or red incision area, foul-smelling discharge, loss of appetite, or profuse diarrhea, as these indicate potential infection or complications like a hernia. Ensure she has access to clean, potable water immediately, and protect the incision site from dust, flies, and contact with bedding to prevent premature closure issues. Once she shows clear signs of recovery and a large appetite returns to her normal hay diet, you can slowly re-introduce small amounts of high-quality grain or concentrated feed to prevent ruminal acidosis.",
      "source": "target",
