      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Systemic signs like a low-grade fever, lethargy, or sudden reluctance to eat can indicate deeper internal issues like an abscess or foreign body migrating, even if the incision looks clean. When in doubt, your best bet for an early diagnosis is taking her to a vet sooner rather than later for a physical exam and possibly an ultrasound to check for unexpected fluid collections or masses. Most recovery complications are best prevented by strict confinement and a calm environment while she heals.",
